 union blending, Separating Axis Theorem (SAT) distance tracking, and Signed Distance Fields (SDF). This provides a more generalized morphing solution that supports rectangles with varying border radii - https://t.co/yWyt8IcEus","id_str":"2063811161230102985","is_quote_status":false,"lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"possibly_sensitive_editable":true,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":12,"retweet_count":16,"retweeted":false,"user_id_str":"901553379490512896"},"note_tweet":{"is_expandable":true,"note_tweet_results":{"result":{"entity_set":{"hashtags":[],"smarttags":[],"symbols":[],"timestamps":[],"urls":[],"user_mentions":[]},"id":"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNjM4MTExNjExNDYxNjcyOTY=","richtext":{"richtext_tags":[]},"text":"Finally, for the SVG liquid glass effect, I implemented Inigo Quilez's smooth union blending, Separating Axis Theorem (SAT) distance tracking, and Signed Distance Fields (SDF). This provides a more generalized morphing solution that supports rectangles with varying border radii - including circles when the border radius is set to 100%.

Additionally, I improved the glass morphing performance to reach 60 FPS by simplifying coordinate rotation calculations, replacing slow lighting approximations, and deferring complex reflections to only calculate along the borders where the glass actually bends.

Also added shadow and border for the glass, and now I have a solid foundation to build upon! 😄"}}},"previous_counts":{"bookmark_count":0,"favorite_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"rest_id":"2063811161230102985","source":"<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>","unmention_data":{},"views":{"count":"19650","state":"EnabledWithCount"},"twe_private_fields":{"created_at":1780885899000,"updated_at":1783835818642,"media_count":1}}

